  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 859 AM MST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nHigh pressure will persist through the week, bringing warmer and \ndrier conditions. Temperatures are expected to run 5-10 degrees \nabove normal through at least Friday. A quick moving system to \nour north will bring increased cloud cover on Tuesday, as well \nas maybe some breezy winds across northeast Utah and northwest \nColorado. \n\nModels indicate the potential for several low pressure systems \nacross the Western CONUS this weekend into next week. Each of \nthese waves have the potential to bring cooler and wetter \nconditions to our area. The first arrives this weekend, and \nprecipitation amounts are not terribly concerning. In general \nthe snow levels appear to range from 7-9 kft, which is lower \nthan previous storms. Beyond that model agreement remains poor \nthis far out, so be sure to stay tuned to see how the forecast \ndevelops over the coming days.",
